              "text": "The symbols on the wall.",
              "outcome": "A good place to start.",
              "next": "t1-s2-c1"
            },
            {
              "id": "b",
              "text": "The people who made them.",
              "outcome": "We will come to that. First, the symbols themselves.",
              "next": "t1-s2-c1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "t1-s2-c1",
          "type": "context",
          "title": "Adinkra",
          "text": "Adinkra are visual symbols associated with the Akan peoples of West Africa. Each symbol stands for an idea or a proverb. They appear on cloth, pottery, walls and many other things.",
          "unlocksCodex": [
            "codex-adinkra"
          ],
          "next": "t1-s2-n2"
        },
        {
          "id": "t1-s2-n2",
          "type": "line",
          "speaker": "Elder",
          "text": "Come, there is one more place I want to show you.",
          "next": null
        }
